    "title": "Paediatric Trauma and Life Support",
    "subtitle": null,
    "summary": "Dr Emaduddin Siddiqui, Associate Professor, Emergency Medicine conducted a workshop on Paediatric Trauma and Life Support for the hospital's post graduate trainees.",
    "media": [
      {
        "_uid": "530ecccad7f55477",
        "component": "news_media",
        "role": "banner",
        "filename": "2762-BannerImage.jpg",
        "src": "/news-media/2762-BannerImage.jpg",
        "media_type": "image",
        "caption": null,
        "alt": "Paediatric Trauma and Life Support"
      }
    ],
    "body": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Managing trauma in the paediatric\npopulation requires specialised skills and expertise. On the 8th of\nOctober 2021, Dr Emaduddin Siddiqui, Associate Professor, Emergency Medicine conducted\na workshop on Paediatric Trauma and Life Support for the hospital's post\ngraduate trainees."
            },
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "After a comprehensive set of lectures from a\nrange of speakers from the Department of Emergency Medicine, Paediatrics and\nSurgery, participants practiced clinical techniques such as needle thoracostomy,\nintraosseous line insertion, and a variety of airway management manoeuvres on our\ntop-notch simulators.\n\n\n\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
